# Registry for `secret seed` / `secret ls`: one "<name> <op://ref> [@account]"
# per line. Names are what configs read at runtime via `secret get <name>`
# (OS keychain, ~30ms, no TTY). Re-run `secret seed` after rotating anything
# in 1Password.
#
# The ref runs to the end of the line, so item and field names may contain
# spaces unquoted. An optional trailing `@<account>` picks the 1Password
# account (shorthand, sign-in address, account ID or user ID — see
# `op account list`). Give it whenever more than one account is signed in:
# vault names such as "Private" are not unique across accounts, and without
# it op resolves against OP_ACCOUNT or its own default account.
#
# homebrew-github-token       op://Private/homebrew/token @my.1password.com
# davmail-password            op://Private/work-o365/password @my.1password.com
# google-api-client-id        op://Private/google-api/client_id @my.1password.com
# ntfy-topic                  op://Private/ntfy/topic @my.1password.com
# other-account-tokenn        op://Employee/other-account/password @work.1password.com
